---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro'
import { getRelativeLocaleUrl } from '@/services/links'

const locale = Astro.locals.locale
const content = {
  title: `${Astro.locals.runtimeConfig.public.brand} | Fair-use policy`,
  description: 'Fair use for Capgo storage, update bandwidth, and observability. What is included, how excessive usage is reviewed, and how prepaid credits work.',
}
---

<Layout content={content}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-24">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-white">Fair-use policy</h1>
    <div class="prose prose-invert mt-8">
      <p>Last updated: November 6, 2026</p>
      <p>
        Paid Capgo plans include bundle storage, update bandwidth, and Observe for normal app development and production use, subject to this policy. MAU and native build time
        remain metered according to your plan. Fair use does not remove those allowances.
      </p>

      <h2 id="storage-and-bandwidth">Storage and bandwidth</h2>
      <p>
        Store the bundles and assets you need to release, operate, and roll back your apps. Deliver updates to your app users as often as needed. Paid plans have no automatic
        storage or bandwidth overage charges and do not block uploads or downloads at the former storage or bandwidth quotas.
      </p>
      <p>
        Keep unused-bundle retention appropriate for your release history. Capgo is not a general-purpose file host, backup service, or CDN for unrelated content. Repeated uploads
        of unused bundles, artificial download traffic, and attempts to bypass service controls fall outside fair use.
      </p>

      <h2 id="observability">Observability</h2>
      <p>
        Observe, app health signals, device logs, and Logs Insights are included for production monitoring, release checks, and troubleshooting. Fair use applies to event volume,
        log collection, retention, queries, and exports, including requests made through APIs or AI agents. It does not promise unlimited event ingestion, indefinite retention, or
        unrestricted queries.
      </p>
      <p>
        Avoid leaving verbose debug logging enabled across your entire user base, streaming unrelated telemetry, repeatedly exporting the full dataset, or polling large date ranges
        at high frequency. Filter queries by app, version, device, and time range when investigating an issue. Existing retention, request-size, and rate limits still apply.
      </p>

      <h2 id="review">How we handle excessive usage</h2>
      <p>
        We review sustained usage that is disproportionate to normal app operation or affects service reliability. We consider your app's active users, release frequency, bundle
        sizes, and the purpose and frequency of observability requests. We contact you to explain the issue and agree a solution, such as changing retention, reducing debug events,
        or adjusting automated queries.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not automatically convert fair-use usage into overage charges. Any custom commercial arrangement requires your agreement. We may rate-limit or temporarily restrict
        abusive usage to protect the service, including before contacting you when immediate action is necessary.
      </p>

      <h2 id="credits">Accounts without a subscription</h2>
      <p>
        If you use prepaid credits without an active paid plan, storage and bandwidth remain metered and consume credits, along with MAU and build time. The storage and bandwidth
        inclusion described above applies to paid subscriptions. Observability remains subject to this policy wherever it is available.
      </p>
      <p>
        See <a href={getRelativeLocaleUrl(locale, 'pricing')}>pricing</a> for allowances and credit rates, and our
        <a href={getRelativeLocaleUrl(locale, 'aup')}>acceptable use policy</a> for other service rules. Contact <a href="https://support.capgo.app">support</a> to discuss a
        workload that may need a custom arrangement.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
